2025-07-15 01:51:47 | INFO     | api.endpoints.qa:generate_sse:402 - [EVENT_DEBUG] 收到事件: <class 'dict'> - {'type': 'knowledge_sources', 'data': {'knowledge_sources': [{'id': '1355b4d6-abdd-44b2-99db-72854f1e58e1', 'content': '问题: 地聚物材料的压缩强度随水铝比的增加呈现何种趋势？这种趋势对材料的实际应用意味着什么？\n答案: 地聚物材料的压缩强度随着水铝比（H2O/Al2O3）的增加而显著下降。例如，当水铝比从10.3增加到18.3时，压缩强度从约85 MPa降低到约40 MPa。尽管强度有所下降，但即使是水铝比最高的样品，其压缩强度（~40 MPa）仍高于普通波特兰水泥（~35 MPa）。这表明地聚物在作为药物载体应用时，仍能保持足够的机械完整性，有效防止因机械冲击导致的“剂量倾泻”风险。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚物材料的压缩强度随水铝比的增加呈现何种趋势？这种趋势对材料的实际应用意味着什么？...', 'score': 0.9070358700000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': ''}, {'id': '948e7f2e-13f4-41d9-bed3-852c595a029d', 'content': '问题: 观察地聚合物材料的压缩强度与密度的关系，呈现出怎样的趋势？解释其原理。\n答案: 地聚合物的压缩强度与密度呈现正相关趋势。例如，GP02具有最高的压缩强度17.25 N/mm2和相对较高的密度约1.86 g/cm3，而发泡样品如GP03密度约0.95 g/cm3，压缩强度仅为1.8 N/mm2。密度越高，通常意味着材料内部的孔隙率越低，结构越致密。致密的微观结构能够更好地承受外部载荷，减少应力集中点，从而提高材料的压缩强度。', 'title': 'QA: 观察地聚合物材料的压缩强度与密度的关系，呈现出怎样的趋势？解释其原理。...', 'score': 0.9003105800000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': ''}, {'id': 'b889f03f-7f1b-4f6d-82d7-68bb5e41acbc', 'content': '问题: 地聚合物的性能，特别是抗压强度，与原材料的整体化学组成（如SiO2或Al2O3的总含量）之间是否存在强相关性？这说明了什么？\n答案: 研究表明，地聚合物的性能（如抗压强度）与原材料的整体化学组成（如SiO2或Al2O3的总含量）之间存在较差的相关性。这意味着仅仅依靠原材料的总体化学组成来预测地聚合物的反应活性或最终性能价值不大。更重要的因素是材料的矿物含量、玻璃相含量和组成，以及这些活性组分在碱性介质中的溶解能力，这些才是真正控制地聚合物化反应和强度发展的关键。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚合物的性能，特别是抗压强度，与原材料的整体化学组成（如SiO2或Al2O3的总含量）之间是否存在...', 'score': 0.89886095, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': ''}, {'id': '86c96933-c794-48e3-a661-9f0ebba706ec', 'content': '问题: 对于地聚合物的抗压强度，固化温度、固化期和碱浓度这三个因素中，哪一个被认为是主导因素？其依据是什么？\n答案: A：固化温度被认为是影响地聚合物抗压强度的最主要因素。实验结果表明，无论碱浓度和固化期如何，地聚合物的抗压强度对固化温度的升高（从20°C到60°C）表现出最显著的响应，例如10M NaOH、3天固化期时，强度从20°C的约3 MPa大幅提升至60°C的31.88 MPa。在较高固化温度（如60°C和80°C）下，即使使用较低的碱浓度或较短的固化期，也能获得较高的抗压强度（约30 MPa），这说明高温能更有效地促进地聚合物化反应，导致离子活性增强和致密结构形成，其影响远超碱浓度和固化期。', 'title': 'QA: 对于地聚合物的抗压强度，固化温度、固化期和碱浓度这三个因素中，哪一个被认为是主导因素？其依据是什么？...', 'score': 0.8429532, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': ''}, {'id': '9cfb5aac-1625-4628-822c-ac5575f3342f', 'content': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\mathrm{{mass}}\\% {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'title': '', 'score': 0.05, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'domain_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition s', 'original_tokens': 539, 'general_tokens': 539, 'domain_tokens': 421, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土<mark>压</mark>力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。']}}], 'knowledge_stats': {'total_sources': 5, 'source_types': {'qa_dataset': 4, 'document': 1}, 'average_score': 0.7198321200000001, 'search_time': 0.0}, 'agent_name': 'cailiao_zhuanjia', 'timestamp': 1752515507.831229}}
